SPEC (fill=S, insert AFTER the P1 end-marker line, still above `function makeJet()`):
Author two functions returning THREE.CanvasTexture, generated once (pattern like makeSpriteTexture @7692). NO fetches.
buildJetSkinTexture(): canvas 1024x1024, ctx.
  - base fill #6d7580 (matches matFuse tint so .map*color stays neutral); overlay 3-4 soft camo blocks in #5f6771 and #7a828d (rounded rects, ~180-320px, low-contrast).
  - panel lines: 1px strokes rgba(30,34,40,0.55) on an irregular grid — verticals every ~90px, horizontals every ~120px, jittered +/-12px.
  - rivet rows: dot rows rgba(40,44,52,0.5) r=1.2 spaced 14px ALONG each panel line.
  - livery accents (O5 grey+orange, NOT clown): two orange #d9721f stripes ~18px tall across upper band; roundel = orange ring + grey center r~46 at (300,300) and (720,700); stencil text 'ELEMENT-115' (orange, 22px bold) near (120,150); tail code 'E-115' (light-grey, 34px) near (860,120); thin off-white anti-slip walkway strip beside centerline.
  return new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas); set .wrapS=.wrapT=THREE.RepeatWrapping.
buildJetRoughTexture(): canvas 512x512, mid-grey #808080 base; redraw ONLY the same panel-line grid darker (#5a5a5a) so seams read rougher; return THREE.CanvasTexture (RepeatWrapping).
>>>
