<<<P11
SPEC (fill=S): Rewrite makeGear(isNose, side=0) richer BUT keep the exact userData contract and the 3 instantiations unchanged.
Structure per gear group `grp`:
  const strutH = isNose ? 1.3 : 1.6, wheelR = isNose ? 0.22 : 0.30;
  strut = new THREE.Group()  // load-bearing; frame code drives its position.x/y + rotation.z
    - outer strut: CylinderGeometry(0.08,0.08, strutH*0.6, 8) matDark, y = -strutH*0.30
    - polished piston: CylinderGeometry(0.05,0.05, strutH*0.55, 8) new MeshStandardMaterial({color:0xb8bcc0, metalness:0.95, roughness:0.15}) [ONE shared const, hoist above makeGear], y = -strutH*0.72
    - scissor link: 2x BoxGeometry(0.02,0.18,0.02) matDark, angled rotation.x = +/-0.5, on the front face
    - drag brace: BoxGeometry(0.035,0.035,0.5) matDark angled rotation.x=0.6 up toward fuselage
    strut.position.y = -strutH/2;
  wheel = new THREE.Group()  // frame code spins rotation.x + sets position.x/y
    - tire: TorusGeometry(wheelR*0.72, wheelR*0.30, 8, 16) matTire, rotation.y = Math.PI/2 (axle along X so rotation.x rolls it)
    - hub: CylinderGeometry(wheelR*0.42, wheelR*0.42, 0.16, 12) polishedMat, rotation.z = Math.PI/2
    - brake disc: CylinderGeometry(wheelR*0.5, wheelR*0.5, 0.03, 16) matDark, rotation.z = Math.PI/2, x offset 0.1
    - 6 bolt studs: tiny CylinderGeometry(0.015,0.015,0.05,6) matDark in a ring on the hub face
    - if isNose: build TWO such wheel sub-groups at x = +/-0.13 and add BOTH to `wheel` (twin nose wheels); mudguard = BoxGeometry(0.4,0.03,0.5) matDark above them
    wheel.position.y = -strutH;
  bay doors (parented to grp, NOT strut, so retract rotation animates them): 2x BoxGeometry(0.5,0.02,0.7) matFuse at grp top, angled ~0.4 rad open.
  grp.add(strut); grp.add(wheel); grp.add(...doors);
CONTRACT (verbatim, unchanged semantics):
  grp.userData.strut = strut;
  grp.userData.wheel = wheel;
  grp.userData.side = side;
  grp.userData.baseStrutY = strut.position.y;
  grp.userData.baseWheelY = wheel.position.y;
  return grp;
KEEP the 3 calls + positions exactly: gearNose=makeGear(true,0) @ (0,-0.6,-4.2); gearL=makeGear(false,-1) @ (-1.8,-0.4,1.2); gearR=makeGear(false,1) @ (1.8,-0.4,1.2); root.add each.
>>>
